po"><country>JP</country><doc-number>11001485</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="XE" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-11001530-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>11001530</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="XE"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7173178-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7173178</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1055674A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> </non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DOW CORNING TORAY SILICONE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA HARUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORITA YOSHITSUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHITAKE MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DOW CORNING TORAY SILICONE CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA, HARUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORITA, YOSHITSUGU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHITAKE, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA HARUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORITA YOSHITSUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHITAKE MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA, HARUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORITA, YOSHITSUGU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHITAKE, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A branched siloxane/silalkylene copolymer which contains a radical-polymerizable organic group and is represented by the general formula (I) [wherein Y is a radical-polymerizable organic group; R&lt;1&gt; is C1-10 alkyl or aryl; and X&lt;1&gt; is silylalkyl represented by general formula (II) where i=1:(wherein R&lt;1&gt; is the same as defined above; R&lt;2&gt; is C2-10 alkylene; R&lt;3&gt; is C1-10 alkyl; X&lt;i+1&gt; is one member selected from the group consisting of hydrogen, C1-10 alkyl, aryl, and the silylalkyl; i, indicating the hierarchial position of the silylalkyl, is an integer of 1 to 10; and a&lt;i&gt; is an integer of 0 to 3)]; and a silicone-containing organic polymer obtained by polymerizing the copolymer.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un copolymère ramifié de siloxane/silalkylène comprenant un groupe organique polymérisable radicalaire, représenté par la formule générale (I). Dans ladite formule, Y est un groupe organique polymérisable radicalaire; R&lt;1&gt; est alkyle C1-10 ou aryle; et X&lt;1&gt; est silylalkyle représenté par la formule générale (II) dans laquelle i = 1. Par ailleurs, R&lt;1&gt; est tel que défini ci-dessus; R&lt;2&gt; est alkylène C2-10; R&lt;3&gt; est alkyle C1-10; X&lt;i+1&gt; peut être hydrogène, alkyle C1-10, aryle et silylalkyle; i, qui donne la position hiérarchique de silylalkyle, est un entier valant de 1 à 10; et a&lt;i&gt; est un entier valant de 0 à 3. L'invention concerne en outre un polymère organique à base de silicone, qui résulte de la polymérisation du copolymère.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>